{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Image credits · {{ site_name }}{% endblock %}
{% block description %}Photographers, licences and source pages for every machine picture on this site.{% endblock %}
{% block content %}

<h1>Image credits</h1>
<p class="lede">
    Four of the machine pictures on this site began as freely licensed
    photographs taken by someone else. This page is where they are credited —
    and where the other fifteen are declared for what they are.
</p>

<p>
    The photographs are not shown as they were taken. Each one was cropped to
    a common shape and put through a cel-shading filter — the
    texture smoothed away, the colour reduced to a small palette, the edges
    inked back in — so that a page of machines reads as one set. The
    processing is
    <a href="{{ contribute_url }}">reproducible from the repository</a>; the
    photographs beneath it are the photographers' work.
</p>

<p>
    A picture made from someone else's photograph is not licensed under this
    site's own CC BY-SA 4.0: it keeps the licence of the photograph it was
    made from, listed below, and an adaptation of a CC BY-SA photograph stays
    under that same licence. Reuse those under their own terms, and keep the
    credit with the image.
</p>

<p>
    Most of the pictures are not photographs at all. Every machine except the
    Commodore 128 and the three compact Macintoshes is a generated
    illustration, marked as such in the table below and in the alt text of
    every appearance. Read them as placeholders for the shape of the machine,
    never as a record of what a particular case, port or board looks like —
    nothing in the dataset is derived from them, and a capacitor list is never
    checked against a picture.
</p>

<table class="credits">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th scope="col">Machine</th>
            <th scope="col">Photograph by</th>
            <th scope="col">Licence</th>
            <th scope="col">Source</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        {% for photo in photos %}
        <tr>
            <th scope="row"><a href="{{ base }}{{ photo.machine_id }}/index.html">{{ photo.machine_name }}</a></th>
            <td>{{ photo.author }}{% if photo.generated %} <span class="meta">(generated illustration)</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td>
                {% if photo.licence_url %}<a href="{{ photo.licence_url }}">{{ photo.licence }}</a>{% else %}{{ photo.licence }}{% endif %}
            </td>
            <td>
                {% if photo.source_url %}<a href="{{ photo.source_url }}">Wikimedia Commons</a>{% else %}—{% endif %}
            </td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
</table>

<p class="meta">
    Cropped and cel-shaded by this project. A machine with no row here has no
    picture at all, and its frame on the site says so.
</p>

{% endblock %}
